  "title": "World Bank Group Invests in Africa's Digital Commerce Infrastructure to Support Jobs and Small Businesses (IFC)",
  "summary": "<strong>Washington, D.C.</strong>, August 12, 2026 — The World Bank Group is supporting the expansion of Africa's digital commerce infrastructure to help small businesses reach new markets, create jobs, and strengthen economic opportunities across the continent. Through Jumia (NYSE: JMIA), Africa's leading e-commerce platform, the investment is expected to enable approximately 60,000 local annual active sellers to participate more fully in the digital economy, support around 1,800 direct jobs, and create income-generating opportunities for more than 100,000 independent sales agents.",
